-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extra:

* If -s is greater than -n, then -s becomes at most -n
* Negative values are rejected
* Default execution with no arguments:

  ./oss

Defaults to:

* -n 1
* -s 1
* -t 1
* -i 0.1

A shared header file (shared.h) was used to store shared structures and constants, improving readability and reducing code duplication.

